(* expect:
buildId is non-empty: true
buildId first byte > 0: true
*)
(* #74/#165 D3: the node names its own build, so a reader can pick the matching
   .oimg.methods.json sidecar. A mismatched sidecar resolves nothing and looks
   identical to a quiet program — this is the field that removes the chance to
   get it wrong by hand. Asserts SHAPE, not the value: the value changes every
   build, and a test that pinned it would fail on every rebuild.

   This dialect has no `isString` predicate — kernel.nsl's only builtin type
   predicates are isValue/isSymbol/isList/isMap/isRecord/isBytes, none of
   which cover String — so the shape is asserted the way the brief's fallback
   prescribes: `size` (non-empty) and `at:` (a String answers a byte SMI
   0..255 for any in-range index; that is the behaviour that actually
   distinguishes a String from every other sized value). *)
class BuildIdTest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | b |
    b:: platform buildId.
    ('buildId is non-empty: ', (b size > 0) printString) println.
    ('buildId first byte > 0: ', ((b at: 1) > 0) printString) println.
    ^ 0 )
) : ()
